<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ reports NZ$406.5 mln trade surplus in May.</title>
<headline>NZ reports NZ$406.5 mln trade surplus in May.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Thursday released the following provisional statistics for New Zealand external merchandise trade for May.</p>
<p>Economists surveyed by Reuters had expected on average a surplus of NZ$293.5 million in May, and a deficit of $563.3 million in the year to May.</p>
<p>(Figures are rounded, with revised-from data in brackets)</p>
<p>Monthly series:</p>
<p>		May 1997	    Apr 1997		May 1996</p>
<p>Balance    +$406.5 million	 +$55.3 million	    +$327.1 million</p>
<p>Exports     $2.09 billion     $1.96 bln	     $2.17 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.68 billion     $1.91 bln	     $1.85 bln</p>
<p>		Yr-to-May 1997    Yr-to-Apr 1997     Yr-to-May 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$460.6 million     -$540.1 million(-$541.1) -$642.6 million</p>
<p>Exports     $20.84 bln	$20.93 bln ($20.93)  $20.70 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $21.30 bln	$21.47 bln ($21.47)  $21.34 bln</p>
<p>Trend series:</p>
<p>		May 1997	    Apr 1997	     May 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$158.1 million    -$141.5 million (-$197.2) -$74.2 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.68 billion  $1.68 bln ($1.65)     $1.73 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.83 billion  $1.82 bln ($1.85)     $1.80 bln</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
